Package: crug
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/cleg0078/crug
Description: Crug: ownership, goroutines and safe types for C
 Crug is a dialect of C, implemented as a fork of GCC 16.2.0, that adds
 Rust-style ownership with automatic destruction, borrows with non-lexical
 lifetimes, goroutines, channels, structured scope and safe core types to
 ordinary C.  It keeps the GNU C dialect and the C ABI unchanged: every
 Crug option is opt-in and a program without Crug constructs compiles to
 the same object code as with the unmodified compiler.
 .
 This package installs the Crug compiler driver (crugc), the C front end
 and the GCC internals it needs, the C headers and libgcc, the Crug runtime
 headers (include/crug) and the static Crug runtime library (libcrug.a).
 .
 Compile a C program with "crugc file.c -o prog"; add the Crug options for
 ownership and the rest, for example "crugc -fcrug-ownership file.c -o prog".
 Runtime programs link the static library: "crugc -fcrug-goroutines file.c
 -lcrug -pthread -o prog".
